ent-ClothingPantsSplintlegs = brigandine chausses
    .desc = Splint mail and brigandine chausses, designed to protect the legs while still providing almost complete free range of movement.

ent-ClothingPantsBplatelegs = blacksteel plate chausses
    .desc = Tasseted leggings of blacksteel, adorned with hooks to suspend both sabatons-and-faulds alike. Besilken trousers shepherd the maille, leaving the royal flesh unmarred by even the slightest of chafes-or-bruises. May its wearer never kneel again; be it in surrender or death.

ent-ClothingPantsIronsplintlegs = splinted leggings
    .desc = A pair of leather pants backed with iron splints, offering superior protection while remaining lightweight.

ent-ClothingPantsChainLeggings = steel chain chausses
    .desc = A set of maille-armored trousers, composed from interlinked steel rings.

ent-ClothingPantsPlateLeggings = steel plate chausses
    .desc = Armored leggings, covered in segmented plates of steel. The trouseres beneath are lined with quilted cloth, ensuring that neither pintle-nor-gudgeon shall succumb to the motions-of-war.

ent-ClothingPantsChainhose = steel chain hosen
    .desc = A set of maille-armored leggings, composed from interlinked steel rings and lightly padded for comfort. Worn in conjunction with one's shortclothes to cover the lower body, the maille socks pair nicely with custom-fitted sabatons. For those seeking to flaunt more regal colors, it can be combined with a pair of cloth hosen.

ent-ClothingPantsChainkilt = steel chain kilt
    .desc = An ankle-length maille skirt, warding cuts against the thighs without slowing the feet.

ent-ClothingPantsUpchainhose = steel chain hosen with coverings
    .desc = A set of maille-armored leggings, composed from interlinked steel rings and lightly padded for comfort. Worn in conjunction with one's shortclothes to cover the lower body, the maille socks pair nicely with custom-fitted sabatons. For a more personalized look, a second pair of cloth hosen has been secured to cover the maille.
